.TH RUSTYMUSICSHEETS 1 "November 2026" "RustyMusicSheets 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustymusicsheets \- sheet music library and performance reader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustymusicsheets
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
RustyMusicSheets is a native Linux application for organizing PDF/PNG/JPEG sheet music,
watching a music folder, creating setlists, and viewing scores during performance.
With no arguments it opens the desktop interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display available commands.
.TP
.BI "\-\-import " PATH
Import a PDF/PNG/JPEG or recursively import supported scores from a folder.
Return a nonzero exit status if any files fail.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List scores in the library.
.TP
.BI "\-\-detect\-instruments " [ID]
Create offline instrument proposals for all scores, or the specified score ID.
Uses PDF text extraction first, then Tesseract OCR when needed.
Review and apply proposals in Library options; this command does not assign them.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Check availability of Poppler PDF helpers and Tesseract.
.TP
.B \-\-smoke\-test
Open the desktop interface and close it after three seconds.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the metadata database and default managed score storage.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for saved preferences.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory reserved for disposable application cache data.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/rustymusicsheets/
.br
.I ~/.config/rustymusicsheets/preferences.json
.PP
A selected music folder stores score files separately from application metadata.
.SH NOTES
Folder watching runs while the application is open.
Use the Library section to choose a music folder and configure readable titles.
F11 toggles fullscreen; Escape leaves performance mode.
Arrow keys and PageUp/PageDown turn pages.
.PP
Settings contains an opt-in keep-awake control to inhibit screen dimming,
idle timeout, and suspend while the application is running.
Inhibitors are released on disable or exit; system policies may override them.
Missing folder-picker starting directories fall back to the user's home.
.PP
The Setlists toolbar button opens management controls for saved setlists
and collections, including rename, duplicate, reorder, add/remove, and
confirmed deletion. Removing a list never removes score PDFs.
.PP
Library displays a large central score browser with search and filters.
Selecting a score opens the separate full-width Reader tab.
Options toggles the library sidebar; returning to Library retains search state.
Page-turn shortcuts apply only in Reader.
Dialogs are constrained to the current window and scroll when necessary.
.PP
Settings and metadata reuse the left sidebar in place of Library options.
Explicit Rescan imports files and removes confirmed missing-score records
after creating a metadata backup. Automatic watching does not delete records.
Rescan never deletes PDFs; unavailable folders and backup failures prevent cleanup.
.PP
Instrument metadata supports multiple instruments, subtypes, and parts.
Library options provides detection and evidence review; Settings controls
opening pages and OCR language. English data is included in package dependencies.
Additional languages require corresponding Tesseract language packages.
The instrument filter and search use assigned metadata, not unconfirmed proposals.
Manual choices, including intentionally empty choices, are protected.
Optional detection for new GUI imports fills only clear, unassigned,
unprotected instruments. Bare Alto/Tenor/Bass labels require review.
No files are uploaded or modified by detection.
.PP
PNG and JPEG images are single-page scores; image-sequence assembly is not supported.
Images exceeding safety limits or with invalid contents are rejected.
Existing databases receive a metadata backup before instrument-schema migration.
.PP
Help provides a searchable offline topic tree, keyboard reference, and About
details (application version, author, and release year). F1 opens help;
Escape or Close help returns to the previous workspace without losing drafts
or reading position. Page-turn shortcuts are suspended in help.
.PP
Instrument detection may take a while for large libraries, especially scans
and images requiring OCR. Warnings appear beside detection controls and before
CLI detection. Background progress and cancellation are available in the GUI.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdfinfo (1),
.BR pdftoppm (1),
.BR pdftotext (1),
.BR tesseract (1)
